{Not available. The opening was a Centre Game [Scandinavian] according to the
Yorkshire Post, 22 April 1922, which puts Tregaskis's name first, suggesting
that he was White (other secondary sources show Maroczy as White). It then
says, "A Centre Gambit offered by Tregaskis was soon refuted by Maroczy, who
won without much difficulty." Depends on the definition of 'Centre Gambit' but
maybe this indicated the Danish Gambit (1 e4 e5 2 d4 exd4 3 c3, etc) in which
case Tregaskis would probably have been White. JS}  0-1

